{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1 — confirmed at runtime)\n\n**Mechanism.** One line: `src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py:63`\n\n    lo = max(1, line_start)\n    hi = line_end if line_end and line_end >= lo else len(lines)\n\nThe `else` branch is the tool's documented \"read to EOF\" fallback for `line_end == 0`, but the\nguard that selects it, `line_end and line_end >= lo`, is false for **two disjoint** inputs: the\ndocumented sentinel (`line_end == 0`) and a **malformed inverted range** (`0 < line_end < lo`,\nor a negative `line_end`). Both therefore land on `len(lines)`. An agent that asks for a bounded\nwindow whose end precedes its start is silently handed the whole rest of the file, capped at\n`_READ_MAX_LINES`, with nothing in the return value distinguishing that from the window it asked\nfor.\n\n**Runtime confirmation.** Driving the real closure (40-line fixture, py3.12, worktree at\n63db6ac5a8):\n\n```\nread_file(\"f.txt\", 5, 8)   -> 4 lines:  \"5\\tline5\" … \"8\\tline8\"          (normal window, correct)\nread_file(\"f.txt\", 15, 8)  -> 26 lines: \"15\\tline15\" … \"40\\tline40\"      (INVERTED -> silent EOF)\nread_file(\"f.txt\", 38, 0)  -> 3 lines:  \"38\\tline38\" … \"40\\tline40\"      (documented sentinel, correct)\n```\n\nThe middle row is the defect, observed executing: a request for an 8-line-ending window returned\neverything to end of file, with no error and no marker. This is the same shape the ticket\nreported live — `read_file(<path>, line_start=115, line_end=30)` issued 31 times by the looping\nverifier in bf31, each returning the same ~11,000-char blob.\n\nThe third row is the discriminator: it rules out the rival explanation that the `else` branch is\nsimply mis-guarded in general, or that `lo`'s `max(1, …)` clamp is at fault. The documented\n`line_end == 0` sentinel behaves exactly as specified, so the defect is precisely and only the\n**inverted** case sharing that branch.\n\n**Legitimacy: `defect`.** The behaviour violates a cited, deliberate, and very recent contract in\nthis same module:\n* commit **85805e02f1** (\"bf31: search_files must not fake `(no matches)`\", 2026-08-05) fixed\n  exactly this class in the sibling tool — \"telling the agent a literal is absent when it was\n  never looked for\" — and its remedy is the one this ticket asks for: \"a path that is neither\n  file nor directory returns an explicit `Error: …`\".\n* the invariant is written into the tool contract the agent is given, at\n  `pai_tools.py:100-105`: search_files returns \"`(no matches)` when the text is genuinely\n  absent, or `Error: …` when `path` cannot be searched — **an error is never reported as\n  `(no matches)`**\".\n* bf31's commit message records why it matters here specifically: these are the read-only tools\n  every rebar LLM gate hands its agent, and a gate that SIGNS its verdict can be driven to a\n  false verdict by a tool that answers a request it did not perform.\n\nThis ticket was created as a deliberate scope carve-out from that fix, by its author, to keep\nbf31's review surface to one function.\n\n**Caller-dependency gate: clear.** `read_file` is a closure built by `filesystem_tools` and\nhanded to Pydantic AI agents (`pai_tools.py:167`). Its only in-repo references are the tool-name\nmemoization set (`agent_call.py:39`), the prompt text describing it (`operations.py:212-215`),\nand reviewer prompt docs. No code branches on the return value's shape, and nothing depends on\nan inverted range meaning EOF — the callers are LLM agents, for whom the current behaviour is\nthe harm, not a contract.\n\n**Fix size:** the change is ~5 non-test lines, far below the 150-line non-test floor of the\nGerrit bugfix-size attestation gate (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:3`), so no\nplan-review attestation is required for this change."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786106956753089001,"uuid":"e90a872d-85cb-4c58-85da-49f45a37217b"}